data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Validated recipe — rainbowkit@2.2.11\n_human-validated 2026-08-11 by farseen (github: FarseenSh)_\n_source: recipes/rainbowkit/wallet-connector.yaml_\n\n**Receipts** — what was actually run, on 2026-08-11, by farseen (github: FarseenSh)\n- checks: attest, test\n- chains exercised: ethereum, base\n- on-chain:\n  - none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.\n\n# Recipe: rainbowkit @2 :: wallet-connector\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-11 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 21 offline · 13 quotes · 0 failures · checklist 4 PASS + 1 OBSERVED. chains [ethereum, base], the two a connection was actually established on. Stamp commit 9ac207b. (Bookkeeping repair 2026-08-12: the fields and the stamp commit below were always the record; this banner had not been flipped. No new validation — session log.)\nproject_id: \"rainbowkit\"    # the PUBLISHER name — never carries the major\nversion_major: 2            # the coexisting-majors key\nversion: \"2.2.11\"           # the exact pin authored against\ntype: \"wallet-connector\"\n\nchains: [ethereum, base]\n\ndeployments: {}\n# A wallet connector performs no token approval. Empty by fact (SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §4).\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Extracted verbatim by test/rainbowkit/extract-recipe.ts and compiled by the harness — the\n# shipped bytes are the bytes that run. Recipe #1's D-1 is why.\nworking_example:\n  source_protocol: \"rainbowkit\"\n  source_url: \"https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/packages/rainbowkit/src/config/getDefaultConfig.ts\"\n  code: |\n    // ── config.ts ──\n    import { getDefaultConfig } from '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit';\n    import { base, baseSepolia, mainnet } from 'wagmi/chains';\n    import { http } from 'wagmi';\n\n    export const config = getDefaultConfig({\n      appName: 'Web3 Context Demo',\n      // REQUIRED. A real id from https://cloud.reown.com — a placeholder disables\n      // every WalletConnect-backed wallet in the modal. See common_mistakes #5.\n      projectId: import.meta.env.VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID,\n      chains: [mainnet, base, baseSepolia],\n      // Pass transports EXPLICITLY. Omit this and every chain silently gets a bare\n      // http() pointing at a public default RPC. See common_mistakes #6.\n      transports: {\n        [mainnet.id]: http(),\n        [base.id]: http(),\n        [baseSepolia.id]: http(),\n      },\n      ssr: false,\n    });\n\n    // ── main.tsx ──\n    import { StrictMode } from 'react';\n    import { createRoot } from 'react-dom/client';\n    import { WagmiProvider } from 'wagmi';\n    import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query';\n    import { RainbowKitProvider } from '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit';\n\n    // NOT optional and NOT auto-injected. Without it the modal renders unstyled.\n    // See common_mistakes #3.\n    import '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/styles.css';\n\n    import { config } from './config';\n    import { App } from './app';\n\n    const queryClient = new QueryClient();\n\n    // The nesting order is load-bearing, not stylistic: RainbowKitProvider calls wagmi's\n    // useAccountEffect internally, so it MUST be inside WagmiProvider, and wagmi's hooks\n    // need the query client. See common_mistakes #4.\n    createRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(\n      <StrictMode>\n        <WagmiProvider config={config}>\n          <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n            <RainbowKitProvider>\n              <App />\n            </RainbowKitProvider>\n          </QueryClientProvider>\n        </WagmiProvider>\n      </StrictMode>,\n    );\n\n    // ── app.tsx ──\n    import { ConnectButton } from '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit';\n    import { useAccount } from 'wagmi';\n\n    export function App() {\n      const { address, isConnected, chain } = useAccount();\n\n      return (\n        <main>\n          <ConnectButton />\n          {isConnected && (\n            <p>\n              connected: {address} on {chain?.name} ({chain?.id})\n            </p>\n          )}\n        </main>\n      );\n    }\n\n# ── INTERFACE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Language-tagged per SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §1 (D15). RainbowKit ships no Solidity.\ninterface:\n  lang: \"typescript\"\n  body: |\n    // @rainbow-me/rainbowkit 2.2.11 — the surface a wallet-connector integration uses.\n\n    // getDefaultConfig builds a wagmi Config with RainbowKit's connectors pre-wired.\n    // It OMITS wagmi's `client` and `connectors` from this type — but the Omit is TYPE-LEVEL\n    // ONLY: at runtime a `connectors` array is accepted and silently replaces every RainbowKit\n    // wallet, because user parameters are spread after them. See common_mistakes #7.\n    function getDefaultConfig(params: {\n      appName: string;                  // typed required — but NOT enforced at runtime (#5)\n      projectId: string;                // typed required AND enforced: omitting it throws (#5)\n      chains: readonly [Chain, ...Chain[]];\n      transports?: Record<number, Transport>;   // omit and EVERY chain gets bare http()\n      appDescription?: string;\n      appUrl?: string;\n      appIcon?: string;\n      wallets?: WalletList;\n      walletConnectParameters?: RainbowKitWalletConnectParameters;\n    }): Config;\n\n    // Must be nested INSIDE WagmiProvider — it calls wagmi's useAccountEffect internally.\n    function RainbowKitProvider(props: {\n      children: ReactNode;\n      initialChain?: Chain | number;\n      theme?: Theme;                    // a theme OBJECT; passing the function throws\n      modalSize?: 'compact' | 'wide';\n      locale?: Locale;\n    }): JSX.Element;\n\n    function ConnectButton(props?: {\n      label?: string;\n      accountStatus?: 'full' | 'avatar' | 'address';\n      chainStatus?: 'full' | 'icon' | 'name' | 'none';\n      showBalance?: boolean;\n    }): JSX.Element;\n\n    // The stylesheet is a SEPARATE subpath export. Nothing imports it for you.\n    // import '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/styles.css';\n\nrequired_imports:\n  - \"@rainbow-me/rainbowkit@2.2.11\"\n  - \"wagmi@^2.9.0        # ⚠ NOT v3 — RainbowKit 2.x cannot install with it\"\n  - \"viem@2.x            # resolves 2.55.11; viem is major 2, never 3\"\n  - \"@tanstack/react-query@>=5.0.0\"\n  - \"react@>=18 · react-dom@>=18\"\n  - \"import '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/styles.css'   # a separate subpath export\"\n\n\n_… recipe truncated for budget — 29437 bytes total, full text at the source path above._\n_Continue it: `web3_fetch` with `cursor: \"recipe:rainbowkit@2.2.11::wallet-connector::body@5970\"` — each call returns the next slice and the next cursor until there is none._\n\n**Citations** (preserved through truncation — degrade bodies, never citations):\n- https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/packages/rainbowkit/src/config/getDefaultConfig.ts\n- https://cloud.reown.com\n- https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/pull/2627\n- https://www.npmjs.com/package/@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/v/2.2.11\n- https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/packages/rainbowkit/package.json\n- https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/packages/rainbowkit/src/components/RainbowKitProvider/RainbowKitProvider.tsx\n- https://www.npmjs.com/package/@reown/appkit/v/1.7.8\n\n---\n\n### 986bf14b-f35e-51d2-b85d-c970f7026e9a\n`rainbowkit@latest` · repo:03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e · as_of 2026-05-06T08:16:28Z\nhttps://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/en-US/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L326-L330\n\n```\nMigration Guide › Migrating RainbowKit › 0.9.x Breaking changes › 1. Upgrade RainbowKit and `wagmi` to their latest version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.9.0 wagmi@^0.9.0\n```\n```\n\n### 752ce3b6-33f1-5094-b0db-c38682dc0551\n`rainbowkit@latest` · repo:03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e · as_of 2026-05-06T08:16:28Z\nhttps://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/en-US/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L344-L348\n\n```\nMigration Guide › Migrating RainbowKit › 0.8.x Breaking changes › 1. Upgrade RainbowKit and `wagmi` to their latest version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.8.0 wagmi@^0.8.0\n```\n```\n\n### ba6de124-dd30-59c2-a3f3-78eba97430c5\n`rainbowkit@latest` · repo:03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e · as_of 2026-05-06T08:16:28Z\nhttps://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/en-US/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L250-L254\n\n```\nMigration Guide › Migrating RainbowKit › 0.12.x Breaking changes › 1. Upgrade RainbowKit and `wagmi` to their latest version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.12.0 wagmi@^0.12.0\n```\n```\n\n### 70e37d42-0b0b-54a3-afe6-42017873c1c1\n`rainbowkit@latest` · repo:03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e · as_of 2026-05-06T08:16:28Z\nhttps://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/en-US/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L290-L294\n\n```\nMigration Guide › Migrating RainbowKit › 0.11.x Breaking changes › 1. Upgrade RainbowKit and `wagmi` to their latest version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.11.0 wagmi@^0.11.0\n```\n```\n\n### 9d598cdd-38cc-5e69-886a-6400be55dc81\n`rainbowkit@latest` · repo:03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e · as_of 2026-05-06T08:16:28Z\nhttps://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/en-US/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L308-L312\n\n```\nMigration Guide › Migrating RainbowKit › 0.10.x Breaking changes › 1. Upgrade RainbowKit and `wagmi` to their latest version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.10.0 wagmi@^0.10.0\n```\n```\n\n### 94283265-3442-52d4-a636-4bb05901584c\n`rainbowkit@latest` · repo:03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e · as_of 2026-05-06T08:16:28Z\nhttps://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/fr/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L326-L330\n\n```\nGuide de migration › Migration de RainbowKit › 0.9.x Modifications importantes › 1. Mettez à jour RainbowKit et `wagmi` à leur dernière version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.9.0 wagmi@^0.9.0\n```\n```\n\n### a4c3431a-f067-5dfb-952d-a50cd1ba1976\n`rainbowkit@latest` · repo:03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e · as_of 2026-05-06T08:16:28Z\nhttps://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/fr/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L344-L348\n\n```\nGuide de migration › Migration de RainbowKit › 0.8.x Modifications importantes › 1. Mettez à jour RainbowKit et `wagmi` à leur dernière version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.8.0 wagmi@^0.8.0\n```\n```\n\n### c87d3af6-c820-5b33-a373-ffd57d606fe3\n`rainbowkit@latest` · repo:03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e · as_of 2026-05-06T08:16:28Z\nhttps://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/fr/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L250-L254\n\n```\nGuide de migration › Migration de RainbowKit › 0.12.x Modifications importantes › 1. Mettez à jour RainbowKit et `wagmi` à leur dernière version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.12.0 wagmi@^0.12.0\n```\n```\n\n### 96b3403b-d5e8-53ce-8831-3d3b46ff2339\n`rainbowkit@latest` · repo:03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e · as_of 2026-05-06T08:16:28Z\nhttps://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/fr/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L290-L294\n\n```\nGuide de migration › Migration de RainbowKit › 0.11.x Modifications importantes › 1. Mettez à jour RainbowKit et `wagmi` à leur dernière version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.11.0 wagmi@^0.11.0\n```\n```\n\n### d39ebf89-fce7-5be6-9f49-f6a6cf8df879\n`rainbowkit@latest` · repo:03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e · as_of 2026-05-06T08:16:28Z\nhttps://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/fr/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L308-L312\n\n```\nGuide de migration › Migration de RainbowKit › 0.10.x Modifications importantes › 1. Mettez à jour RainbowKit et `wagmi` à leur dernière version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.10.0 wagmi@^0.10.0\n```\n```"}],"structuredContent":{"intent":"integrate","recipe":{"project_id":"rainbowkit","version":"2.2.11","recipe_type":"wallet-connector","last_validated":"2026-08-11","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","receipts":{"validated_on":"2026-08-11","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","checks":["attest","test"],"chains_exercised":["ethereum","base"],"on_chain":"none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result."},"body":"# Recipe: rainbowkit @2 :: wallet-connector\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-11 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 21 offline · 13 quotes · 0 failures · checklist 4 PASS + 1 OBSERVED. chains [ethereum, base], the two a connection was actually established on. Stamp commit 9ac207b. (Bookkeeping repair 2026-08-12: the fields and the stamp commit below were always the record; this banner had not been flipped. No new validation — session log.)\nproject_id: \"rainbowkit\"    # the PUBLISHER name — never carries the major\nversion_major: 2            # the coexisting-majors key\nversion: \"2.2.11\"           # the exact pin authored against\ntype: \"wallet-connector\"\n\nchains: [ethereum, base]\n\ndeployments: {}\n# A wallet connector performs no token approval. Empty by fact (SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §4).\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Extracted verbatim by test/rainbowkit/extract-recipe.ts and compiled by the harness — the\n# shipped bytes are the bytes that run. Recipe #1's D-1 is why.\nworking_example:\n  source_protocol: \"rainbowkit\"\n  source_url: \"https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/packages/rainbowkit/src/config/getDefaultConfig.ts\"\n  code: |\n    // ── config.ts ──\n    import { getDefaultConfig } from '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit';\n    import { base, baseSepolia, mainnet } from 'wagmi/chains';\n    import { http } from 'wagmi';\n\n    export const config = getDefaultConfig({\n      appName: 'Web3 Context Demo',\n      // REQUIRED. A real id from https://cloud.reown.com — a placeholder disables\n      // every WalletConnect-backed wallet in the modal. See common_mistakes #5.\n      projectId: import.meta.env.VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID,\n      chains: [mainnet, base, baseSepolia],\n      // Pass transports EXPLICITLY. Omit this and every chain silently gets a bare\n      // http() pointing at a public default RPC. See common_mistakes #6.\n      transports: {\n        [mainnet.id]: http(),\n        [base.id]: http(),\n        [baseSepolia.id]: http(),\n      },\n      ssr: false,\n    });\n\n    // ── main.tsx ──\n    import { StrictMode } from 'react';\n    import { createRoot } from 'react-dom/client';\n    import { WagmiProvider } from 'wagmi';\n    import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query';\n    import { RainbowKitProvider } from '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit';\n\n    // NOT optional and NOT auto-injected. Without it the modal renders unstyled.\n    // See common_mistakes #3.\n    import '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/styles.css';\n\n    import { config } from './config';\n    import { App } from './app';\n\n    const queryClient = new QueryClient();\n\n    // The nesting order is load-bearing, not stylistic: RainbowKitProvider calls wagmi's\n    // useAccountEffect internally, so it MUST be inside WagmiProvider, and wagmi's hooks\n    // need the query client. See common_mistakes #4.\n    createRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(\n      <StrictMode>\n        <WagmiProvider config={config}>\n          <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n            <RainbowKitProvider>\n              <App />\n            </RainbowKitProvider>\n          </QueryClientProvider>\n        </WagmiProvider>\n      </StrictMode>,\n    );\n\n    // ── app.tsx ──\n    import { ConnectButton } from '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit';\n    import { useAccount } from 'wagmi';\n\n    export function App() {\n      const { address, isConnected, chain } = useAccount();\n\n      return (\n        <main>\n          <ConnectButton />\n          {isConnected && (\n            <p>\n              connected: {address} on {chain?.name} ({chain?.id})\n            </p>\n          )}\n        </main>\n      );\n    }\n\n# ── INTERFACE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Language-tagged per SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §1 (D15). RainbowKit ships no Solidity.\ninterface:\n  lang: \"typescript\"\n  body: |\n    // @rainbow-me/rainbowkit 2.2.11 — the surface a wallet-connector integration uses.\n\n    // getDefaultConfig builds a wagmi Config with RainbowKit's connectors pre-wired.\n    // It OMITS wagmi's `client` and `connectors` from this type — but the Omit is TYPE-LEVEL\n    // ONLY: at runtime a `connectors` array is accepted and silently replaces every RainbowKit\n    // wallet, because user parameters are spread after them. See common_mistakes #7.\n    function getDefaultConfig(params: {\n      appName: string;                  // typed required — but NOT enforced at runtime (#5)\n      projectId: string;                // typed required AND enforced: omitting it throws (#5)\n      chains: readonly [Chain, ...Chain[]];\n      transports?: Record<number, Transport>;   // omit and EVERY chain gets bare http()\n      appDescription?: string;\n      appUrl?: string;\n      appIcon?: string;\n      wallets?: WalletList;\n      walletConnectParameters?: RainbowKitWalletConnectParameters;\n    }): Config;\n\n    // Must be nested INSIDE WagmiProvider — it calls wagmi's useAccountEffect internally.\n    function RainbowKitProvider(props: {\n      children: ReactNode;\n      initialChain?: Chain | number;\n      theme?: Theme;                    // a theme OBJECT; passing the function throws\n      modalSize?: 'compact' | 'wide';\n      locale?: Locale;\n    }): JSX.Element;\n\n    function ConnectButton(props?: {\n      label?: string;\n      accountStatus?: 'full' | 'avatar' | 'address';\n      chainStatus?: 'full' | 'icon' | 'name' | 'none';\n      showBalance?: boolean;\n    }): JSX.Element;\n\n    // The stylesheet is a SEPARATE subpath export. Nothing imports it for you.\n    // import '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/styles.css';\n\nrequired_imports:\n  - \"@rainbow-me/rainbowkit@2.2.11\"\n  - \"wagmi@^2.9.0        # ⚠ NOT v3 — RainbowKit 2.x cannot install with it\"\n  - \"viem@2.x            # resolves 2.55.11; viem is major 2, never 3\"\n  - \"@tanstack/react-query@>=5.0.0\"\n  - \"react@>=18 · react-dom@>=18\"\n  - \"import '@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/styles.css'   # a separate subpath export\"\n","source_path":"recipes/rainbowkit/wallet-connector.yaml","requested_version":null,"exact_version_match":null,"body_truncated":true,"body_bytes":29437,"citations":["https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/packages/rainbowkit/src/config/getDefaultConfig.ts","https://cloud.reown.com","https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/pull/2627","https://www.npmjs.com/package/@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/v/2.2.11","https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/packages/rainbowkit/package.json","https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/packages/rainbowkit/src/components/RainbowKitProvider/RainbowKitProvider.tsx","https://www.npmjs.com/package/@reown/appkit/v/1.7.8"],"citations_capped":false,"body_cursor":"recipe:rainbowkit@2.2.11::wallet-connector::body@5970"},"hits":[{"selector":"986bf14b-f35e-51d2-b85d-c970f7026e9a","source_url":"https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/en-US/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L326-L330","snippet":"Migration Guide › Migrating RainbowKit › 0.9.x Breaking changes › 1. Upgrade RainbowKit and `wagmi` to their latest version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.9.0 wagmi@^0.9.0\n```","project":"rainbowkit","version":"latest","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-13T03:54:35Z","as_of":"2026-05-06T08:16:28Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e"},{"selector":"752ce3b6-33f1-5094-b0db-c38682dc0551","source_url":"https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/en-US/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L344-L348","snippet":"Migration Guide › Migrating RainbowKit › 0.8.x Breaking changes › 1. Upgrade RainbowKit and `wagmi` to their latest version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.8.0 wagmi@^0.8.0\n```","project":"rainbowkit","version":"latest","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-13T03:54:35Z","as_of":"2026-05-06T08:16:28Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e"},{"selector":"ba6de124-dd30-59c2-a3f3-78eba97430c5","source_url":"https://github.com/rainbow-me/rainbowkit/blob/03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170348e/site/data/en-US/docs/migration-guide.mdx#L250-L254","snippet":"Migration Guide › Migrating RainbowKit › 0.12.x Breaking changes › 1. Upgrade RainbowKit and `wagmi` to their latest version\n```bash\nnpm i @rainbow-me/rainbowkit@^0.12.0 wagmi@^0.12.0\n```","project":"rainbowkit","version":"latest","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-13T03:54:35Z","as_of":"2026-05-06T08:16:28Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"03360ee924cfa6af13ff1d623b356bf5a170